hus accosted harshly, Vibhisana, speaking truth, rose up along with four Rākṣasas having maces in their hands.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-16-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6010012","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f1cd2ca81793b88aa373e73ed62fb0396d3831ccb795f84fc7a9b2f29cf9f33e","compact":"16752825a1107597745d59c287ee27d6078aaa8ed2466b9f4c869b2ac343be63","nasal":"16752825a1107597745d59c287ee27d6078aaa8ed2466b9f4c869b2ac343be63"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-10-13","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":10,"verse":13,"english":"There upon, rising up in the welkin, the graceful brother Vibhisana, worked up with ire, addressed the lord of Rāshasas.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.788,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-16-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6010013","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cbdf429ad601bec1d433a523408750398d2bd4d626071036d66a4b5ad5036a9f","compact":"a4612be9781e82de460771e5a84781df8a2db817bec5bd62df4b44d218ca2817","nasal":"b40bd17fcfe9242a4c656cc01886caa63c6f7aede0ee1c65408d731ea17fb4f3"}},{"id":"VRCE-6-10-14","kanda":6,"kandaId":"yuddha","sarga":10,"verse":14,"english":"You are mistaken, O king. Do you speak what you wish, you are my elder brother, adorable like to father-you did not follow the track of virtue. I cannot tolerate the harsh accents of you, my elder brother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.578,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-6-16-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"6010014","sanskritFile":"Ram06.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b89e8d55fc302accf1725dbfcbcb026bd9ec500acbcff4fcf4e8a7ab869bd703","compact":"3eb14c8a321a92b59e93b3407ff7e5d18af56d753210cad9988ac7d1eb0e0304","nasal":"3e